                <p class="dateAesteticTitle2 center">Dimitri Fontaine is debuting in new Vilpa Max Animated Series Blue
                    Shades</p>
            </div>
            <div class="col s12 m2"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col s12 m2"></div>
            <div class="col s12 m8 paragraphStyleNews">
                <h4 class="bolderFont">
                    The Vilpa Talents actor discusses his first acting role, finding himself in Hassan, and why growth
                    begins long before you feel ready.
                </h4>
                <p>For Dimitri Fontaine, every new chapter begins the same way... with a challenge.</p>
                <p>After spending the last ten years building a career as a fitness coach, Fontaine is now preparing for
                    an entirely different stage as he makes his acting debut in Blue Shades, Vilpa Films' upcoming
                    original animated series.</p>
                <p>
                    Rather than seeing the transition as a leap into the unknown, he sees it as something much simpler.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <span class="bolderFont" style="font-style: italic;">"I live for challenges! Everything starts this
                        way."</span>

                </p>
                <P>It was that mindset that first led him to audition for Hassan, one of the series' central characters.
                </P>

                <hr>
                <h5 class="bolderFont">Finding Himself in Hassan</h5>
                <p>
                    Set in a future where human artists have been criminalised, Blue Shades follows Elisa and Hassan as
                    they challenge <span class="bolderFont">KREATIVA</span>, an artificial intelligence entertainment
                    megacompany that controls artistic expression.
                </p>
                <p>When asked what first drew him to Hassan, Fontaine didn't mention action or adventure. Instead, he
                    spoke about the character's way of thinking.</p>
                <p>
                    <span class="bolderFont" style="font-style: italic;">"He understands society and how the world
                        works, but he knows he has to stay smart to win against this new kind of society."</span>
                </p>
                <p>Another aspect immediately stood out to him.</p>
                <p>
                    <span class="bolderFont" style="font-style: italic;">"I was also interested in being an outlaw, but
                        for the truth, for the right things."</span>

                </p>
                <p>Preparing for the role meant looking inward as much as outward.</p>
                <p>Drawing from his own experiences, Fontaine connected moments from his life with Hassan's emotional
                    journey while studying other characters who shared a similar mindset.</p>
                <p>
                    <span class="bolderFont" style="font-style: italic;">"I took some parts of myself with my own
                        experience... To complete my character, I inspired myself by studying other characters with the
                        same kind of mindset."</span>

                </p>
                <hr>
                <h5 class="bolderFont">Learning a New Craft</h5>
                <p>Although acting represents a completely new profession, Fontaine believes many of the skills he
                    developed as a coach naturally carried over into performance.</p>
                <p>
                    <span class="bolderFont" style="font-style: italic;">Vilpa Films asked how he adapted to acting
                        after years in coaching.</span>

                </p>
                <p>His answer was immediate.</p>
                <p>
                    <span class="bolderFont" style="font-style: italic;">"I use skills that I've earned during my
                        coaching career in the acting field, like reading and understanding the emotions of other
                        people. It helps me to understand my character."</span>

                </p>
                <p>
                    Even the way he watches films has changed.
                </p>
                <span class="bolderFont" style="font-style: italic;">"Now, when I'm watching a movie, I want to analyze
                    everything I can about the actor to understand how I can take some specific things to add them to my
                    skills."</span>

                <hr>
                <h5 class="bolderFont">Joining Vilpa Talents</h5>
                <p>Through Blue Shades, Fontaine also became part of Vilpa Talents, Vilpa Films' international
                    initiative supporting actors, filmmakers and creatives working across its productions.
                </p>
                <p>Asked what the experience has meant to him, he described it as both motivating and humbling.</p>
                <p>
                    <span class="bolderFont" style="font-style: italic;">"That's just amazing! Since my casting for
                        Hassan, everything has passed so fast! That's an honor for me to have my name next to the big
                        names of this industry."</span>

                </p>
                <p>But beyond the opportunity itself, joining the initiative strengthened his commitment to the craft.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <span class="bolderFont" style="font-style: italic;">"To be recruited on Vilpa Talents makes me want
                        to work harder because I know that I'm able to be so many different characters. That's literally
                        what I love—to be completely a different person."</span>

                </p>
                <hr>
                <h5 class="bolderFont">Every Character Is an Opportunity to Grow</h5>
                <p>Although Fontaine continues running his coaching company, he is clear about where he hopes this new
                    journey will lead.</p>
                <p>
                    <span class="bolderFont" style="font-style: italic;">"My long-term goal is to go as far as possible
                        in the film industry!"</span>

                </p>
                <p>For him, acting is more than performance.</p>
                <p>It's personal growth.</p>
                <p>
                    <span class="bolderFont" style="font-style: italic;">"Every character is a new challenge, an
                        opportunity to learn new things for yourself through your character. So every time I play a
                        character, I grow as a man too."</span>

                </p>
                <p>He also believes that Vilpa Films and Vilpa Max can become important platforms for emerging actors
                    looking to build international careers.</p>

                <p>
                    <span class="bolderFont" style="font-style: italic;">"They give me the chance to be seen by people
                        and other producers to make them want me to play their next main character in future
                        productions."</span>

                </p>
                <hr>
                <h5 class="bolderFont">Why Blue Shades Matters</h5>
                <p>Beyond its dystopian world, Fontaine believes audiences will connect with Blue Shades because its
                    characters reflect emotions everyone has experienced.</p>
                <p>
                    <span class="bolderFont" style="font-style: italic;">"We all have known an unfair or hard event in
                        our life."</span>

                </p>
                <p>He hopes viewers will stand beside Hassan and Elisa throughout their journey while becoming immersed
                    in the visual world the production is creating.</p>
                <p>
                    <span class="bolderFont" style="font-style: italic;">"The production is working hard to get the best
                        kind of animation and atmosphere... They will have the impression they can take part in the
                        story too."</span>

                </p>
                <hr>
                <h5 class="bolderFont">The Advice He Wishes Every Artist Would Hear</h5>
                <p>Before ending our conversation, we asked Fontaine what advice he would give to artists wondering
                    whether they should pursue their creative ambitions.</p>
                <p>His response reflected the same philosophy that has guided his own path into acting.</p>
                <p>
                    <span class="bolderFont" style="font-style: italic;">"One of the most important things that I've
                        learned is to do it without feeling ready to do it, because you will always feel doubt, fear,
                        anxiety or some feelings which make you give up."</span>

                </p>
                <p>He recalls that during the production of Blue Shades, Alejandro Vilpa encouraged him to step beyond
                    acting itself—even inviting him to write and perform the series' theme song.</p>
                <p>Another challenge, another opportunity to grow.</p>
                <p>And perhaps the sentence that best captures both his journey and the spirit of Blue Shades comes in
                    his closing words.</p>
                <p>
                    <span class="bolderFont" style="font-style: italic;">"Nothing is easy but hard work never lies! You
                        have to work smartly and be patient, never ever give up. If you feel it, live it."</span>

                </p>

